    "narrative": "For the May 21st slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 87.14 efficiency score. His matchup against Zach Agnos (5.15 xERA) is the most favorable on the board, and as a primary source of our stolen base production, his placement in the #2 hole maximizes his potential to capitalize on Agnos\u2019s defensive vulnerabilities. Joining him in the top tier, **James Wood** (64.53) provides massive upside despite facing a lefty in David Peterson. His elite xwOBA (.381) and leadoff status largely offset the neutral platoon disadvantage, making him a critical start for Roto categories. Similarly, **Gabriel Moreno** (65.19) is a surprising high-floor play today; the combination of a weak opposing starter and favorable park factors elevates his profile well above his typical output, cementing his spot as our primary catcher.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Tyler Soderstrom** and his 59.99 score. While he remains a strong start, his marginal edge over the rest of the infield pool highlights a crowded depth chart where efficiency gains are razor-thin. We are currently navigating a thin roster due to the IL statuses of **Jose Caballero** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, who remain sidelined. Furthermore, we are managing the absence of **Josh Naylor** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** due to team off-days, effectively shortening our rotation. While **Mickey Moniak** (60.41) and **Kyle Karros** (55.86) remain in the lineup, we must monitor the pending lineups closely; **Mickey Moniak** faces a significant 15% penalty due to the platoon disadvantage against Eduardo Rodriguez, and any shift in his lineup position could rapidly downgrade his utility. We continue to track the minor league production of **Henry Bolte**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Carson Williams** as potential depth reinforcements should these fringe starters falter under today's projected conditions.",
